  "body": "## What changed\n\nRead the live MCP tool list for each provider request.\nMap its schemas to Anthropic Messages, OpenAI Chat Completions, OpenAI Responses, and Gemini generateContent.\nSet OpenAI strict to false.\nConvert Gemini type arrays to anyOf and remove $schema from schema locations.\nPreserve literal enum and default values.\n\nAdd call parsers and result adapters that preserve call IDs and MCP errors.\nValidate tool names and arguments before returning a call.\nAdd local JSON proposals that require explicit confirmation for edits.\nAdd prompt context and read-only Q&A context for models without native tools.\nThe mapper prepares calls and does not execute them.\n\nRecord the choices in docs/decisions/1943-tool-schema-mapper.md.\nThis branch starts at upstream/main cfc8447e.\nEffort: medium. No escalation.\n\n## Cause\n\nThe MCP registry had no provider-format mapper or validated local fallback.\nEach provider needs a different schema and call envelope.\n\n## Tests\n\nThe first pin run failed on unchanged production code with E0432 because mcp::provider did not exist.\nThe nine integration pins now pass:\n\n- every_live_tool_maps_without_schema_loss\n- provider_calls_and_results_keep_the_call_identity\n- prompt_parser_accepts_one_object_and_refuses_untrusted_shapes\n- schema_validation_names_bad_arguments_before_confirmation\n- mutating_fallback_calls_wait_for_explicit_confirmation\n- no_native_tools_selects_the_two_local_fallback_tiers\n- native_calls_refuse_invalid_arguments_and_malformed_json\n- text_responses_have_no_calls_and_parallel_calls_are_preserved\n- native_call_ids_are_required_and_unique_except_optional_gemini_id\n\nSix unit pins also pass:\n\n- gemini_normalization_strips_schema_keywords_and_preserves_literal_data\n- gemini_type_union_preserves_existing_combinators\n- boolean_schemas_and_invalid_schema_shapes_refuse_by_name\n- new_schema_keywords_refuse_authorization_by_name\n- schema_combinators_enforce_their_distinct_match_counts\n- nullable_types_keep_the_literal_enum_constraint\n\nThe old-module mutation restored mcp/mod.rs from git show upstream/main.\nThe pin failed with the missing API, then passed after restoration.\nAll 34 behavior mutations failed with assertions, then passed after restoration:\n\nregistry, required, type, enum, minimum, maximum, minItems, maxItems, items,\nproperties, additionalProperties, confirmation, allowlist, single-json,\nduplicate-id, missing-id, native-validation, missing-input, unsupported-keyword,\nanyOf, oneOf, allOf, gemini-schema, gemini-union, response-shape, response-array,\ncall-type, empty-name, encoded-json, proposal-fields, unclosed-fence,\nboolean-true, boolean-false, schema-shape.\n\ncargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main passed the app library and 79 suites in 330 seconds.\nClippy first found three equivalent assertion-style errors in the new tests.\nAfter their correction, the nine integration pins passed again.\ncargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings passed.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone. git diff --stat upstream/main -- \"*.nc\" \"*.cl\" is empty.\n\n## Not exercised\n\nLive provider requests, streaming responses, and a GUI confirmation flow were not exercised.\nNetwork transport and the confirmation UI are outside this offline mapper change.\nCallers must keep the original response for reasoning items and Gemini thought signatures.\nLiteral schema validation refuses null for set_work_material because its current enum does not contain null.\n\n## Overlaps\n\nPR #1738 touches the same file, different function; whichever merges second refreshes.\nIt adds WCS flip module declarations in crates/app/src/mcp/mod.rs.\nThis PR adds provider module declarations at a different location.\nThe two PRs do not change the same function or lines.\n\nChangelog: Add live MCP schema mapping for Anthropic, OpenAI, and Gemini, with validated local JSON proposals and read-only Q&A context.\n\nFixes #1943\n",
